F]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]An unlabelled task relation is one undirected link, shown [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]everywhere as `🪢 links` with no arrow. A labelled relation is a [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]directed statement read from its source. A bare `~~` asks for a [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]label. Every writer, reader, and client (bob-cli, bob-plugins, Bob [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]Mac Capture) applies the same pair rules on the unchanged LINKS / [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]LINKED FROM storage, so a plain re-add never erases a label and a [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]pair is never listed twice.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]8[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202610/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]undirected_task_relations.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202610/undirected_task_relations.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-am[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-am/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Relation contract, glossary, and decision record[/bold #D7AFFF]              [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]contract[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]contract: rewrite docs/task-relations.md around the pair model [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF](vocabulary, pair rules, projection, writer table, chips, JSON, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]every new or changed vector), update the vocabulary-level docs, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]write the glossary strands and the decision record through [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]/sase_memory_write.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rust pair model, planner, and reconcile projection[/bold #D7AFFF]            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]pair-core[dim] · [dim][/dim]after contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]pair-core: add a pure pair-state and pair-write planner in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]task_relations, stop bare adds from stripping labels, teach reconcile to[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]omit plain mirrors the target already names, and add the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]redundant_relation warning, all pinned by the LW and LR vectors.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Capture grammar, completion, and the label-required reverse [/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]link[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]capture-grammar[dim] · [dim][/dim]after pair-core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]capture-grammar: make a bare `~~` an incomplete draft that submit [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]refuses, add `kind` to parsed relations, make completion symmetric with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]existing_kind/existing_direction, end every `~~` replacement in `|`, add[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the related-label hint, rename the shell groups, and update the capture [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]syntax docs (ships as `feat(capture)!:`).[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Pair-aware capture writers and sentence-shaped output[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]capture-writes[dim] · [dim][/dim]after pair-core, capture-grammar[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]capture-writes: route `~` / `~~` writes through the pair planner in one [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]all-or-nothing batch (no-op re-adds, label conversions, moves, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]both-endpoint mirror deltas), add `kind` and `moved_from` to [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]relation_updates, rewrite the human output as sentences, and update the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]linking docs and guide.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Obsidian pair planner twin, writers, and relations API v2[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]nav-writer[dim] · [dim][/dim]after pair-core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]nav-writer: port the pair planner to bob-navigation-hotkeys with shared [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]vectors, make applyRelationEdit, removeLink, Ctrl+D, and the hand-edit [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]mirror pair-aware with add-before-remove cross-note writes, and publish [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`api.relations` v2 (unlink, removeStatement, reverse openStage).[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]One aggregated links block per task in bob-ledger-tools[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]ledger-chips[dim] · [dim][/dim]after contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]ledger-chips: add the additive `related()` per-task view to [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`api.relationIndex` and render one `🪢 links` block per task (arrow-free[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]plain chips, then statements) in Live Preview and Reading view, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]collapsing the second relation line, with v2-aware × and ＋ controls.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]One Links row and one Links stage with a live label sentence[/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]nav-stage[dim] · [dim][/dim]after nav-writer, ledger-chips[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]nav-stage: merge the Task Card rows and the two relation stages into one[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Links row and stage fed by `related()`, with plain ↵, a ⇧↵ label field [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]showing a live sentence and ⇄ swap, ⇧L as the reverse-label shortcut, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]